1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:04,019
Tired of telling Codex, "Use this style, do it this way,"

2
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:05,270
at the start of every chat?

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:09,450
Here's how to make Codex remember your preferences permanently with one file,

4
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:12,560
so it gets it right without you repeating yourself.

5
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:15,280
So say Codex just made this for me.

6
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:18,460
I like how it turned out, this layout, this style.

7
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:22,160
Normally, I'd have to describe this all over again next time,

8
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:25,020
but instead, I'm just going to tell it to remember it.

9
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:29,040
From now on, whenever I ask for a landing page and I don't specify styling,

10
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:32,460
please use this exact format and style.

11
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,340
Remember this going forward.

12
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:35,075
That's it.

13
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:37,610
I just told it, "Remember this going forward."

14
00:00:38,010 --> 00:00:39,760
And what it's actually doing behind the scenes,

15
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:44,680
it's writing this into a file on your computer called agents.md.

16
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:47,269
That's your manual memory file.

17
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:50,500
Anything you specifically ask it to remember goes in here.

18
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:54,320
Now, let's paste another prompt to open the agents.md.

19
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:58,880
Open the agents.md file for this project and show me what's in it.

20
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:00,820
See that?

21
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:05,150
It literally wrote down what I like, the format, the style, everything,

22
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:08,280
in plain text right here in this file.

23
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:09,840
And here's the best part.

24
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:12,420
This isn't just for one chat.

25
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:16,259
Every new chat you start, Codex reads this file first,

26
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:19,580
so it already knows your preferences before you even ask.

27
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:22,980
And you don't only have to ask the agent to update it,

28
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:29,920
you can literally open this file yourself and edit it directly like a notepad.

29
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:33,940
Add rules, remove ones you don't like anymore, whatever you want.

30
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:38,180
This file is basically your agent's permanent instruction manual

31
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:40,020
for how you like things done.

32
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:45,060
So next time, instead of repeating yourself, just say, "Remember this,

33
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:52,340
check your agents.md file,"and boom, your agent never forgets your style again.

34
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:54,880
Try it out and let me know how it goes.
